I had to react to this - some errors in these spoilers.
Disclaimer: maybe some things *are* correct in 3.0.10, not in 3.0.7
which I've played most.
In article <15351@june.cs.washington.edu> pullen@badger.cs.washington.edu (Walter D. Pullen) writes:
>I never wish for dragon scale mail, because the armor will
>periodically polymorph you into that color of dragon, causing you tear
>out of your cloak (and hawiian shirt if you have one), so in other
>words, combining a cloak of magic resistance with other armor will
>yield a higher AC then gray dragon scale mail.

Untrue, as David Hairston already pointed out. Furthermore, if you
"merge with your armor" (i.e. polymorph into a gray dragon), and then
become human again, you retain the gd scale mail! I suppose this doesn't
happen when you polymorph into a gray dragon without gd scale mail.

> Ring of teleport control:
>    Combine it with a nymph/leprechaun corpse and you can ^T away from trouble.

You don't need the ring to get ^T ability - you do need teleportation,
and more - Exp level 10 as in good old hack, maybe?

>  a blessed tinning kit
>    Good for when satiated and you have a wraith corpse right in front of you.

"This corpse is much to insubstantial to can" (or somesuch). Good for other 
intrinsic-giving corpses (giants!), though. Yesterday I had 11 blessed
tins of tengu meat - I just wanted to make sure I got the intrinsic.

Generally: many objects mentioned with "blessed". I think "blessed" is
only necessary for tools, rings and armor when you're going to encounter
magic-using monsters. For wands, it isn't necessary at all - They say
cursed wands may explode, but it never happened to me.

Otherwise, excellent hints.

BTW, you may remember that in 3.0.7 it was possible to get "infinite"
wishes (from magic lamps, in particular) using polypiling. I tried it
for once - stayed on lvl 3 (altar) for 50.000 turns (expeditions to
dlvl <=8) and finished the game after that with "everything" maxed out -
in some 4000 more turns. It's not much fun, of course.

